s; and at specialty licensing and comic book shows, conventions, and exhibitions, as well as through its e-commerce business. The company was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Everett, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Josh  Simon | CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $823K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Funko, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $336M market cap on $908M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -12% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $38M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 13.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","